1
00:00:00,825 --> 00:00:02,235
Thursday after school.

2
00:00:02,505 --> 00:00:04,185
The quiz papers are back.

3
00:00:04,532 --> 00:00:05,802
One mark out of three?

4
00:00:05,982 --> 00:00:07,562
But my answer was right!

5
00:00:09,912 --> 00:00:11,926
My answers used to lose marks too.

6
00:00:11,946 --> 00:00:14,144
Then I met the Genie in TheOneApp.

7
00:00:14,706 --> 00:00:17,556
A little dragonfly is hiding in this video.

8
00:00:17,806 --> 00:00:19,046
Can you spot it?

9
00:00:19,442 --> 00:00:22,040
Dragonflies love windows and plants.

10
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:23,214
Look outside!

11
00:00:23,633 --> 00:00:25,093
You against the Buddies!

12
00:00:25,363 --> 00:00:27,213
Lock in first with your fingers.

13
00:00:27,483 --> 00:00:29,313
One finger for every point.

14
00:00:29,969 --> 00:00:31,299
Today you'll learn:

15
00:00:31,496 --> 00:00:33,566
The four parts of a full answer.

16
00:00:33,846 --> 00:00:35,536
Evidence from the question.

17
00:00:35,815 --> 00:00:37,585
The concept you remember.

18
00:00:38,089 --> 00:00:39,029
Are you ready?

19
00:00:39,469 --> 00:00:40,239
Three!

20
00:00:40,619 --> 00:00:41,279
Two!

21
00:00:41,649 --> 00:00:42,299
One!

22
00:00:42,719 --> 00:00:43,439
Go!

23
00:00:43,943 --> 00:00:45,293
Here is the question.

24
00:00:45,563 --> 00:00:49,263
Mei Ling hangs two metal bars, X and Y, from strings.

25
00:00:49,543 --> 00:00:52,473
She brings the North pole of a magnet near each bar.

26
00:00:52,733 --> 00:00:54,913
Bar X moves away from the magnet.

27
00:00:55,173 --> 00:00:57,593
Bar Y moves towards the magnet.

28
00:00:57,863 --> 00:00:59,443
Which bar is a magnet?

29
00:00:59,723 --> 00:01:01,043
Explain your answer.

30
00:01:03,056 --> 00:01:03,936
Round one.

31
00:01:04,246 --> 00:01:06,096
Which answer gets full marks?

32
00:01:06,386 --> 00:01:07,566
One, Basil's.

33
00:01:07,856 --> 00:01:08,816
Two, Pip's.

34
00:01:09,116 --> 00:01:10,226
Three, Momo's.

35
00:01:10,516 --> 00:01:11,826
Show me your fingers!

36
00:01:17,344 --> 00:01:18,324
Locked in!

37
00:01:18,602 --> 00:01:19,232
One!

38
00:01:19,372 --> 00:01:20,372
I wrote X.

39
00:01:20,442 --> 00:01:21,572
X is right!

40
00:01:21,926 --> 00:01:25,026
Two. Mine says like poles repel.

41
00:01:25,226 --> 00:01:26,766
That is the science!

42
00:01:27,115 --> 00:01:27,955
Three.

43
00:01:28,095 --> 00:01:29,925
Mine has all four parts.

44
00:01:30,577 --> 00:01:31,617
Be an answer!

45
00:01:31,907 --> 00:01:32,887
Shrink down.

46
00:01:33,167 --> 00:01:34,097
Quietly.

47
00:01:36,383 --> 00:01:39,163
You are an empty answer line in a quiz paper.

48
00:01:39,943 --> 00:01:42,693
A red piece floats down and clicks into place.

49
00:01:43,463 --> 00:01:45,113
Bar X is a magnet.

50
00:01:45,703 --> 00:01:48,493
Then a blue piece: what the question shows you.

51
00:01:49,293 --> 00:01:51,513
A yellow piece: the science rule.

52
00:01:52,273 --> 00:01:56,043
And last, a green piece that joins them all to the question.

53
00:01:56,693 --> 00:02:00,650
The marker's pen comes down.

54
00:02:00,670 --> 00:02:01,469
Tick.

55
00:02:01,489 --> 00:02:02,288
Tick.

56
00:02:02,308 --> 00:02:03,107
Tick.

57
00:02:03,127 --> 00:02:04,874
Full marks!

58
00:02:06,915 --> 00:02:09,365
The answer is three: Momo's answer!

59
00:02:09,625 --> 00:02:11,295
Did you show three fingers?

60
00:02:11,565 --> 00:02:12,975
Put one finger up!

61
00:02:13,376 --> 00:02:14,813
Meet the CECL Genie.

62
00:02:14,833 --> 00:02:18,211
It shows us the four parts of a full answer.

63
00:02:18,915 --> 00:02:20,575
So what did my answer miss?

64
00:02:21,450 --> 00:02:22,600
Look closer.

65
00:02:23,210 --> 00:02:25,650
Basil gave a Choice: bar X.

66
00:02:26,230 --> 00:02:27,810
That is the red part.

67
00:02:28,084 --> 00:02:29,824
But it moved is not enough.

68
00:02:30,404 --> 00:02:32,264
Which way did bar X move?

69
00:02:32,844 --> 00:02:34,324
Away from the magnet.

70
00:02:34,884 --> 00:02:38,124
That is the Evidence, and it comes from the question.

71
00:02:38,411 --> 00:02:42,241
An open-ended question is a question you answer in your own sentences,

72
00:02:42,261 --> 00:02:44,811
such as: which bar is a magnet?

73
00:02:45,171 --> 00:02:46,561
Explain your answer.

74
00:02:47,211 --> 00:02:48,251
Your turn.

75
00:02:48,841 --> 00:02:52,091
What science rule explains why bar X moved away?

76
00:02:52,691 --> 00:02:53,471
Think.

77
00:02:58,094 --> 00:03:01,994
Evidence is what the question shows you, such as: bar X moved

78
00:03:02,014 --> 00:03:03,464
away from the magnet!

79
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:08,050
Say it with me!

80
00:03:08,765 --> 00:03:13,045
A full answer has four parts: Choice, Evidence, Concept and Link.

81
00:03:15,674 --> 00:03:17,274
I know my Concept!

82
00:03:17,474 --> 00:03:19,894
Bar X moves away from the magnet.

83
00:03:20,169 --> 00:03:21,729
Something is not right.

84
00:03:21,999 --> 00:03:24,179
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

85
00:03:24,459 --> 00:03:25,419
Hold on!

86
00:03:30,832 --> 00:03:31,962
Arms crossed?

87
00:03:32,232 --> 00:03:33,442
One finger up!

88
00:03:33,719 --> 00:03:35,729
Pip, that is the question's own words!

89
00:03:35,759 --> 00:03:36,949
That is Evidence.

90
00:03:37,019 --> 00:03:40,559
The Concept is the rule you remember: like poles repel.

91
00:03:40,907 --> 00:03:43,337
So how does Momo's answer fit together?

92
00:03:44,212 --> 00:03:45,362
Look closer.

93
00:03:45,922 --> 00:03:48,832
Choice, in red: Bar X is a magnet.

94
00:03:49,190 --> 00:03:52,850
Evidence, in blue: When the North pole of the magnet was brought

95
00:03:52,870 --> 00:03:55,790
near bar X, bar X moved away.

96
00:03:56,138 --> 00:03:58,988
Concept, in yellow: Like poles repel.

97
00:03:59,568 --> 00:04:02,938
Only a magnet can be repelled by another magnet.

98
00:04:03,295 --> 00:04:07,585
Link, in green: Thus, bar X was repelled, so bar X is

99
00:04:07,605 --> 00:04:08,485
a magnet.

100
00:04:08,846 --> 00:04:12,286
A concept is the science rule you remember, that is true every

101
00:04:12,306 --> 00:04:14,986
time, such as: like poles repel!

102
00:04:15,638 --> 00:04:20,398
Bar Y moved towards it, but a magnet attracts magnetic materials too,

103
00:04:20,468 --> 00:04:22,968
so that does not show Y is a magnet.

104
00:04:25,889 --> 00:04:27,049
Say it with me!

105
00:04:27,759 --> 00:04:29,889
Evidence is what the question shows you.

106
00:04:30,429 --> 00:04:32,809
Concept is the science rule you remember.

107
00:04:35,363 --> 00:04:36,823
Show me your score hand!

108
00:04:37,103 --> 00:04:38,133
Two fingers?

109
00:04:38,413 --> 00:04:39,783
You beat the Buddies.

110
00:04:40,063 --> 00:04:41,063
High five!

111
00:04:41,716 --> 00:04:43,416
Did you spot the dragonfly?

112
00:04:43,696 --> 00:04:45,726
It was on a twig of the tree outside!

113
00:04:46,016 --> 00:04:47,326
Here is a fun fact!

114
00:04:47,396 --> 00:04:50,856
A dragonfly's huge eyes can see almost all the way round its

115
00:04:50,876 --> 00:04:51,506
head.

116
00:04:51,796 --> 00:04:53,906
It gathers evidence from every side!

117
00:04:54,102 --> 00:04:55,382
Tell someone at home!

118
00:04:56,111 --> 00:04:58,311
Let's read today's key words together!

119
00:04:58,601 --> 00:04:59,361
Ready?

120
00:04:59,648 --> 00:05:01,068
Open-ended question.

121
00:05:03,088 --> 00:05:03,948
Evidence.

122
00:05:05,382 --> 00:05:06,292
Concept.

123
00:05:07,814 --> 00:05:08,754
Well done!

124
00:05:09,551 --> 00:05:12,581
Now I want to try a new question, all by myself!

125
00:05:12,854 --> 00:05:14,704
Can you build a full answer too?

126
00:05:14,974 --> 00:05:16,564
Find out in Part Two!

127
00:05:17,829 --> 00:05:18,930
Say it with us!

128
00:05:19,730 --> 00:05:20,480
Ready?

129
00:05:20,604 --> 00:05:21,264
One!

130
00:05:21,604 --> 00:05:22,304
two!

131
00:05:22,609 --> 00:05:23,784
Now you know!
